19:T704,## 1. Requirements

- A **movie** plays as many **shows**, each show is a movie at a given **screen** and **time**.
- Every show has its own **seat map**; a user **selects seats**, **pays**, and gets a **confirmation**.
- The hard rule: the **same seat must never be double-booked**, even when two users tap "Book" at the exact same instant.

State that race up front, it's the entire point of this interview.

## 2. The classes

`Theatre` → `Screen` → `Show` → `Seat` model the venue, plus a `BookingService` that orchestrates and a `Booking` that records a confirmed reservation. A `Screen` **composes** its `Seat`s; a `Show` runs on a `Screen` at a time.

## 3. The crux: a SeatLockProvider

When a user **selects** seats, you don't book them yet, you **LOCK** them with a short **TTL** (e.g. 5 minutes). Only the **lock holder** may pay. On payment the lock becomes a `Booking`; on timeout it **auto-releases** so the seat returns to the pool.

This is the key move: it turns a **check-then-act** race into a single **atomic claim**.

```
boolean acquire(seats, user) {
    // atomic: set heldBy=user, expiry=now+5min
    // ONLY if every seat is currently unlocked
    return store.compareAndSet(seats, FREE, user);
}
```

## 4. Why a naive "isBooked flag" fails

A plain `if (!seat.isBooked) seat.isBooked = true` is a classic race: two threads both **read** `false`, both decide it's free, both **write** `true` → the same seat is booked twice. Read-then-write is not atomic.

## 5. Locking options

- **DB row lock**, `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` on the seat rows inside a transaction.
- **Distributed lock**: Redis `SETNX` with a TTL (works across many app servers).
- **Optimistic concurrency**, a version column; the second writer's `UPDATE … WHERE version = ?` fails and retries.c:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex min-h-screen","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"activeModule":"lld-case-studies","activeLesson":"book-my-show"}],["$","$L18","book-my-show",{"lesson":{"id":"book-my-show","patternId":"lld-case-studies","title":"Design BookMyShow","kind":"case-study","difficulty":"Advanced","statement":"Browse shows, pick seats, and book them, where the whole difficulty is concurrency: two users must never book the same seat.","companies":["Amazon","BookMyShow","Uber","Atlassian"],"theory":"$19","approaches":[{"label":"Model the booking domain","code":["class Show { Movie movie; Screen screen; Time time; }","class Screen { List<Seat> seats; }","","class BookingService {","    SeatLock lock;","    Booking book(List<Seat> seats, User user) { ... }","}"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":1,"narration":"The static model first: a Show runs on a Screen which OWNS its Seats (composition). A BookingService creates Bookings.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"show","name":"Show","fields":["- movie","- time"],"x":0,"y":0.2},{"id":"screen","name":"Screen","fields":["- seats"],"x":1.1,"y":0.2},{"id":"seat","name":"Seat","fields":["- id","- status"],"x":2.3,"y":0.2},{"id":"svc","name":"BookingService","methods":["+ book(seats, user)"],"x":0,"y":1.55,"tint":"accent"},{"id":"lock","name":"SeatLock","fields":["- ttl","- heldBy"],"methods":["+ lock(seats)","+ unlock()"],"x":1.3,"y":1.55,"tint":"red"},{"id":"booking","name":"Booking","fields":["- seats","- user"],"x":2.5,"y":1.55}],"relations":[{"id":"r1","from":"show","to":"screen","kind":"aggregate","label":"runs on"},{"id":"r2","from":"screen","to":"seat","kind":"compose","label":"seats *","toMult":"*"},{"id":"r3","from":"svc","to":"lock","kind":"aggregate","label":"locks"},{"id":"r4","from":"svc","to":"booking","kind":"depend","label":"creates"},{"id":"r5","from":"booking","to":"seat","kind":"assoc"}],"shownClassIds":["show","screen","seat","svc","booking"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2","r4","r5"],"activeIds":["show","screen","seat"]},"vars":[["Show","movie + screen + time"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":5,"narration":"Now spotlight SeatLock (red), the heart of the design. It is a lock with a TTL and a holder, sitting between selecting a seat and booking it.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["show","screen","seat","svc","lock","booking"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2","r3","r4","r5"],"activeIds":["lock"]},"vars":[["SeatLock","ttl + heldBy"]]},{"view":"class","narration":"Selecting seats LOCKS them for a few minutes; only the holder can pay. An unpaid lock auto-expires and frees the seats, so a check-then-act race becomes one atomic claim.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["show","screen","seat","svc","lock","booking"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2","r3","r4","r5"],"activeIds":["lock","svc"]},"vars":[["lock","5 min TTL"],["on pay","lock → Booking"]]}]},{"label":"Flow: two users, one seat","code":["boolean lock(seats, user) {","    // ATOMIC: claim only if all seats are free","    return store.compareAndSet(seats, FREE, user, ttl=5min);","}","// only heldBy == user may pay → confirm"],"steps":[{"view":"sequence","codeLine":1,"narration":"User A selects seat 14. An atomic lock succeeds, the seat is now held by A for 5 minutes.","sequence":{"actors":[{"id":"a","label":"User A","kind":"actor"},{"id":"l","label":"SeatLock","tint":"red"},{"id":"b","label":"User B","kind":"actor"}],"messages":[{"id":"m1","from":"a","to":"l","label":"lock(seat 14)","kind":"call"},{"id":"m2","from":"l","to":"a","label":"locked (5 min) ✓","kind":"return"},{"id":"m3","from":"b","to":"l","label":"lock(seat 14)","kind":"call"},{"id":"m4","from":"l","to":"b","label":"already held ✗","kind":"return"},{"id":"m5","from":"a","to":"l","label":"pay → confirm","kind":"call"}],"shownCount":2,"activeIndex":1},"vars":[["User A","holds the lock → books ✓"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":2,"narration":"At the same moment User B tries to lock seat 14, the atomic lock REJECTS it. B is told the seat is already taken. No double booking, even under a race.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":4,"activeIndex":3},"vars":[["User B","rejected → no double-book ✓"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":5,"narration":"A pays within the window, so the lock converts to a confirmed Booking. Only the lock holder could reach this step.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":5,"activeIndex":4},"vars":[["User A","holds the lock → books ✓"]]},{"view":"sequence","narration":"The lock turned a check-then-act race into a single atomic claim. Had A not paid, the TTL would expire and free seat 14 for B. That is the whole design.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":5,"activeIndex":4},"vars":[["atomic claim","no double-book"],["timeout","frees seat for B"]]}]}]}}]]}]
